    "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Generate one original square 2×2 atlas of four separate pictures for a first-grade mathematics lesson about packing prop pieces backstage. Exactly equal quadrants, tiny plain cream gutter at both center lines, keep images safely within each cell. Flat cut-paper gouache, clean silhouettes, muted sage, warm yellow, terracotta and plum, warm school theatre atmosphere. No lettering, numbers, equation symbols, dots, countable sets of objects, printed textbook material or reference images. Top left: empty school theatre packing room, warm low stage, curtains at the sides, pale open central floor, natural light, no objects in center. Top right: one simple playful green toy packing trolley with shallow empty basket, terracotta handle and dark wheels, side angle, entirely visible on a warm light plain background. Bottom left: one cheerful oversized paper award rosette with blank central circle and two green ribbon tails, on a warm light plain background. Bottom right: a quiet school backstage pathway with soft shadows and light wood sides and lots of open floor, no objects or markings. No marks or elements suggesting specific mathematical quantities. Do not repeat any panel."
